(Bug #95. The other two spellings of an untyped declaration. `the NAME is
 VALUE.` and `NAME is VALUE.` bring a name into being exactly as `Set NAME
 to VALUE.` does, so a text declared either way must read back as its own
 text and not as the address the integer formatter made of it.)

the greeting is "hello".
Print greeting.

motto is "carry on".
Print motto.

the score is 7.
Print score.

roster is ["ann", "bo"].
Print roster.
